    "notes": "Q430792/relation1841091 identifies the precinct; the broad archaeological boundary is a platform extent rather than a solid temple shell. The pinned PMTiles cella35184503447863 and 22 individual perimeter columns plus the southern column-fragment cluster fix the exposed remains. Architecture+X points southeast toward the Colosseum, about20.58degrees from east in native east/south space. The ordinary east frontal photo resolves the open apse direction. Later church/museum footprints are excluded from the platform and replacement mask. Reused pinned N0506 standard PMTiles/Mapzen extract. The broad precinct uses a flat visualization datum just above the sampled perimeter; retaining foundations extend below the unmodified native ground. Later independent building footprints are subtracted from the platform. No ground or water cutout; exact archaeological pavement elevation is not surveyed. The pinned main temple and Antiquarium polygons overlap by about 0.032m². The replacement mask excludes the museum with a0.1mm numerical margin; a tiny native temple seam remains inside/along the museum wall. Preserve that shared seam rather than clip the independent museum. This is map-overlap handling, not an inferred archaeological wall boundary. Reused pinned N0506 standard PMTiles/Mapzen extract. The broad precinct uses a flat visualization datum just above the sampled perimeter; retaining foundations extend below the unmodified native ground. Later independent building footprints are subtracted from the platform. No ground or water cutout; exact archaeological pavement elevation is not surveyed. All 1,634 independent in-tile buildings are unchanged after excluding the museum from the replacement mask. The original main temple and museum footprints overlap by about 0.032m²; the corrected mask preserves the independent museum and leaves 0.03264347m² of native temple geometry at that shared seam, within/along the museum wall. Other temple/column records are replaced to sub-1e-7m² numerical boundary remnants. Native terrain and 3,021.82m² water remain unchanged. Failed loading restores all 1,658 original records; eviction frees geometry."
